WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.003 --> 00:00:02.139
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.503
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.039
between Ben &amp; Jerry's
in the UK and the US.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.273
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.811
In the UK, Ben &amp; Jerry's comes with

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:14.681
a standard tub size of 465 milliliters.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:17.450
And the cores tubs are the same size.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.518
Look at this little cute guy.

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.353
In the US, we start with these mini tubs.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:23.923
They're 118 milliliters, or 4 ounces.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:26.059
A standard US Ben &amp; Jerry's pint

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:29.629
is 16 ounces, or 473 milliliters.

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.131
And also like in the UK,

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:32.799
our cores, this guy right here,

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:35.068
is the same size as our regular pint.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:38.271
Our topped tubs are
actually slightly smaller.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:42.442
They are 15.2 fluid
ounces, or 450 milliliters.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.078
One thing to note is that despite

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.713
the two being very similar sizes,

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:49.082
the UK does not refer
to its tubs as pints.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.483
That's because pints
are actually different

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:51.684
in the UK and the US.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.520
Here in the US, we measure our liquids

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.455
using US customary measurements,

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:58.058
which is based on an
18th-century English –

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:58.992
who cares, all right?

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.727
Our pint is 16 fluid ounces.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.562
In the UK, we use imperial measurements,

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.464
which were only established in 1824,

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:06.399
after the US had declared independence.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.568
Our pints are 568 milliliters,

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.970
which is 1.2 times larger than a US pint.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.038
To illustrate the difference,

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:14.207
I've brought in an
imperial-measurements measuring jug.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.475
We're going to fill it with ice cream.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.212
That just looks like the best milkshake

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.613
you've ever had, honestly.

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:24.617
According to Target,
this is 16 fluid ounces.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:27.520
So we're gonna put this in
here and see what happens.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.456
And in case you still don't believe us,

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.091
this is a British pint glass.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.926
We're gonna fill this with ice cream.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:33.760
Joe: Here we go.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:41.167
While I've got this pint in front of me,

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.936
it would be kind of rude not to try,

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.704
wouldn't it? Cheers.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:45.572
[sighs] All right.

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.046
[Harry laughs]
Joe: Found the walnuts.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:54.447
It was going really
well, then I hit a lump.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.649
I'm down to about here though.
Pretty strong, I think.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.318
[Joe burps]

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.887
It's the lumps that get you. But honestly,

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.489
not the worst way to eat Ben &amp; Jerry's.

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:03.356
I mean, as much as I can get,

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.425
then I gotta start eating
it. How does that look?

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.795
Fun fact: This is
actually how Ryan Gosling

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:11.331
ended up gaining 60
pounds for a movie role,

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:12.398
which he then got fired from.

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:14.134
So, ended up being a little
bit of a waste of time,

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:17.103
but pretty effective way to pile on mass.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.371
Now, while the volume of ice cream you get

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.507
in the two countries is
theoretically pretty similar,

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:21.674
one other thing we wanted to check

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.943
was how much topping you
get mixed in with your tub.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.446
Here's a pint of Cookie Dough in the US.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:28.314
We've let it melt. So
we're going to strain it

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:31.284
to see how many cookie-dough
chunks are in a pint.

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:33.153
We'll do the same over here. Let's go.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.687
Oh, yeah, that ice cream is totally

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:37.357
catching up with me right now.

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:38.691
I swear to God, if I throw up ...

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.193
The style of this reminds me of the net

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:42.428
you use to catch bugs in Animal Crossing,

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.596
with the little ...

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:44.430
whichew!

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:46.933
Joe: Here we go.

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:53.907
Yeah, this is completely
arbitrary. Here we go.

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.275
Doesn't look very appetizing

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.843
when you put it like that, does it?

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:59.712
I have to sift through this, I guess.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:02.115
Yeah, these are all -- one, two ...

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:04.284
Just another day at the
office, really, isn't it?

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.752
12, 13, 14, 15?

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:07.287
So, in a UK tub of Cookie Dough,

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:10.190
we got around 33 pieces
of actual cookie dough

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.424
in varying sizes.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.226
While we're going into excruciating detail

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:14.794
on the portion sizes, why not take a look

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.262
at the cores tubs as well?

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:16.996
[ice cream thuds]

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.398
It's the same flavor in the US.

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:19.732
Let's cut this bad boy open.

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.269
Ha-ha!

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.971
I can still eat this after
I've sawed it in half?

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.673
Is there anything, any chemicals on here

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.708
that are likely to kill me?

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:29.442
We'll find out.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:33.913
[ice cream thuds]

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:37.517
Ooh!

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:40.553
[heavenly music]

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:41.721
That core doesn't go all the way in there.

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:42.922
It's kind of like ...

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:45.858
Chocolate, vanilla, salted caramel core.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:47.860
Just pick it up.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.132
I mean, I didn't wash the saw.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.834
A bit of woody oak flavor.

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:58.438
Here are all the Ben &amp; Jerry's
items you'll find in the UK

00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:00.073
that you won't find in the US.

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:02.842
And here are most, actually half,

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:05.478
of the US-exclusive Ben &amp; Jerry's flavors.

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:06.312
We'll start with this one,

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:08.014
which is the Birthday Cake ice cream.

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:09.015
I haven't actually tried this before,

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:11.117
but apparently it's vanilla
cake batter ice cream

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:13.987
with pink frosting, strawberry
swirls, and cake pieces.

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:15.121
Americone Dream.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.991
This is the Stephen
Colbert-flavored ice cream.

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:19.659
I'm not quite sure what Steve tastes like,

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:22.562
but it looks like they got
his essence in this pint.

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.931
Speaking of ice cream
that is person-flavored,

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:27.567
The Tonight Dough. Look,
you see that right there?

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:30.703
There is absolutely no way

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.505
that's his hand holding that cone.

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:34.007
Good job on the Photoshop, those guys.

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:36.309
The Berry Sweet Mascarpone.

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:38.778
Another one you can
only get here in the US.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:41.147
Would be something – I'll
be straight up with you,

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:42.749
as an Italian man, I'm
about to say something

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:45.151
very controversial, but
this flavor, when I saw it,

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:47.587
I was like, "Yuck! No, thank you."

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:50.990
Where is it? It is literally
the first one in front of me.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.859
Ben &amp; Jerry's Cannoli flavor.

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.961
A "Mascarpone Ice Cream with Fudge-Covered

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:57.297
Pastry Shell Pieces &amp;
Mascarpone Squirrels."

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:58.998
Squirrels. "Swirls."

00:04:58.998 --> 00:04:59.932
Next up, we've got this one,

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:01.768
which is Cookie Dough S'Wich Up.

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:03.736
Next up we've got the Dough-ble Chocolate

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:04.904
Cookie Dough Twist.

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.873
Caramel Chocolate Cheesecake.

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:07.907
This is a no-brainer right here.

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:08.908
I bet this one's pretty good.

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:09.742
"What's in it?" You ask.

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:12.178
"Caramel Cheesecake Ice
Cream with Cheesecake Pieces,

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:14.047
Chocolate Cookie Swirls." Hell yeah, dude.

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:15.815
This is going in the Joe pile.

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.718
Cherry Garcia. They don't
have Cherry Garcia in the UK?

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:19.819
Doesn't that seem weird?

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:22.155
This is, like, when everyone
found out about Ben &amp; Jerry's,

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:23.589
I feel like. Cherry Garcia was –

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.058
I have no idea if this was before

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:27.694
Jerry Garcia died or in tribute of him.

00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:29.729
Chocolate Peanut Butter Split.

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:31.331
I'm gonna assume it's
chocolate and peanut butter.

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.165
What do you guys think?

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:33.199
Chocolate Therapy.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:35.268
"Chocolate Ice Cream
with Chocolate Cookies

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:37.236
&amp; Swirls of Chocolate Pudding."

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.439
Like, every consistency of chocolate.

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:41.040
Ah, the Chubby Hubby.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.375
Thought this one was, like, super popular.

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:46.179
Chunky Monkey was earlier, it
was banana and walnuts and ...

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:47.413
it's the one I drank.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.349
It's not sitting right. Ugh.

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:51.417
Next up we've got Cone Together,

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:53.953
which I'm guessing is
a "Come Together" pun.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.855
Did The Beatles do "Come Together"?

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:57.557
I really, I'm not a Beatles guy.

00:05:57.557 --> 00:06:00.059
I just listen to Owl City,
so I'm not the person

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.994
to come to for classic music advice.

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:03.162
Cinnamon Bun.

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.397
Tastes like cinnamon buns.

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:06.699
Coffee Coffee BuzzBuzzBuzz.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:09.335
Maybe this instead of your
morning coffee. [laughs]

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.270
Coffee Toffee Bar Crunch.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.707
Everything But The dot dot dot.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:15.975
It has a lot of stuff in here.

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:17.610
Gimme S'more.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.245
Glampfire Trail Mix.

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:21.347
Go-To Cold Brew, another coffee one.

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:23.182
Next up we've got Baked Alaska.

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:25.518
Now, I've actually never
eaten a proper baked Alaska,

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:27.253
but I presume it tastes similar to this.

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:28.554
This has got vanilla ice cream

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:31.023
with marshmallow swirls
and white polar bears.

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:33.693
Then we go into the Caramel
Chew Chew ice cream.

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:36.863
New York, baby! Super Fudge Chunk.

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:39.098
Salted Caramel Almond.

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:41.000
Not as many punny ones
as I thought, right?

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.370
Vanilla Caramel Fudge.
I wonder what's in it.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:45.772
Milk and Cookies.

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:47.407
Peanut Butter Half Baked.

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:49.175
So it's a combination of
the two most popular ones.

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:50.510
That's pretty smart, actually.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.812
What? This is crazy! This can't be right.

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:53.713
Vanilla?

00:06:53.713 --> 00:06:55.615
Why don't you have vanilla in the UK?

00:06:55.615 --> 00:06:58.751
Then our lost classic tub
is Sofa So Good Together.

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:00.620
I'm not sure why they
needed the "Together."

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.488
I feel like the pun works
better without the "Together."

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:04.323
Ben &amp; Jerry, if you're
listening, fix this.

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:05.858
The Punch Line.

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:07.226
Chillin' the Roast truffles.

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:09.295
Pistachio Pistachio.

00:07:09.295 --> 00:07:11.164
Oat of this Swirled.

00:07:11.164 --> 00:07:13.065
OK, now we're getting back on the puns.

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:14.667
Strawberry Cheesecake.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:16.803
And this isn't even all of them.

00:07:16.803 --> 00:07:20.573
In the US, you can also
get flavors such as

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:22.575
Boots on the Moooo'n,

00:07:22.575 --> 00:07:23.609
Brewed to Matter,

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:24.877
Chocolate Shake It,

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:26.813
Cold Brew Caramel Latte,

00:07:26.813 --> 00:07:27.880
Ice Cream Sammie,

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.482
Justice ReMix'd,

00:07:29.482 --> 00:07:30.650
Mint Chocolate Cookie,

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:31.951
Peanut Butter World,

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:33.619
Red, White &amp; Blueberry,

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:34.854
Triple Caramel Chunk,

00:07:34.854 --> 00:07:35.688
Urban Bourbon,

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:36.823
Pumpkin Cheesecake,

00:07:36.823 --> 00:07:37.824
Totally Unbaked.

00:07:37.824 --> 00:07:39.225
That's just the regular ones.

00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:40.426
We got a lot more to go through.

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:42.695
We also have a few
nondairy and low-calorie

00:07:42.695 --> 00:07:43.830
exclusives in the UK.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:44.797
We'll start at the end with this one,

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:46.532
which is Save Our Swirled NOW.

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:48.501
Then we have one more nondairy exclusive,

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.603
which is this one:
Cookies on Cookie Dough.

00:07:50.603 --> 00:07:54.106
Here in the US, you can
get the, in nondairy form,

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:56.509
Americone Dream and The Tonight Dough,

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:58.377
"Milk" and Cookies,

00:07:58.377 --> 00:07:59.278
Cherry Garcia,

00:07:59.278 --> 00:08:01.314
Chocolate Caramel Cluster

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:03.049
and Mint Chocolate Cookie,

00:08:03.049 --> 00:08:04.884
Caramel Almond Brittle,

00:08:04.884 --> 00:08:06.018
Crème Brûlée Cookie,

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:08.087
ooh, the Netflix &amp; Chilll'd,

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:09.021
Peanut Butter Half Baked,

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:10.423
and Phish Food.

00:08:10.423 --> 00:08:12.225
A few other flavors you can get in the US

00:08:12.225 --> 00:08:13.826
that you can't get in the UK, nondairy,

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:15.928
that I also couldn't get
in the US but I've assumed

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:17.763
are available somewhere in this country

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:20.500
are the Karamel Sutra Core, nondairy,

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:23.302
the Coconut Seven Layer Bar, nondairy,

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:26.672
and the Coffee Caramel Fudge, nondairy.

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:28.174
Then we're on to some low-calorie options,

00:08:28.174 --> 00:08:30.343
which Ben &amp; Jerry's calls Moo-phoria.

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:33.045
Now, this one up here is
a Chocolate Cookie Dough,

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:34.213
low-calorie version,

00:08:34.213 --> 00:08:37.817
but it's only 136 calories
per 100 milliliters.

00:08:37.817 --> 00:08:39.418
Our next Moo-phoria exclusive flavor

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:41.320
is the Salted Caramel Brownie one.

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:42.922
The next Moo-phoria
exclusive we were able to get

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:44.490
was this one: Poppin Popcorn.

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:47.293
The Moo-phoria light flavors
you can get in the US are:

00:08:47.293 --> 00:08:49.228
Chocolate Cookie Enlightenment.

00:08:49.228 --> 00:08:51.531
[drumroll]
EnlightenMint, M I N T.

00:08:51.531 --> 00:08:53.232
Very good, Ben &amp; Jerry's.

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:54.567
Chocolate Milk and Cookies,

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:55.935
Mocha Fudge Brownie,

00:08:55.935 --> 00:08:57.136
P.B. Marshmallow.

00:08:57.136 --> 00:08:58.437
I am slightly against the concept

00:08:58.437 --> 00:08:59.472
of low-calorie ice cream.

00:08:59.472 --> 00:09:00.973
I feel like with something like this,

00:09:00.973 --> 00:09:03.009
you just have to enjoy it as
it was intended to be enjoyed,

00:09:03.009 --> 00:09:04.744
which is the proper way.

00:09:04.744 --> 00:09:05.811
If you're going to save some calories,

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.880
maybe just save them elsewhere
and then treat yourself,

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.382
or just eat less of one of these

00:09:09.382 --> 00:09:10.516
instead of a whole tub of that.

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:12.485
As you saw when I hacked
one open with a saw,

00:09:12.485 --> 00:09:14.487
Ben &amp; Jerry's also sells cores ice cream,

00:09:14.487 --> 00:09:16.689
which is ice cream flavors with a core

00:09:16.689 --> 00:09:18.824
of usually some kind of
caramel filling in the middle.

00:09:18.824 --> 00:09:20.693
We've only got one exclusive
over here, which is this one,

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:22.528
the Blondie Brownie Core.

00:09:22.528 --> 00:09:24.397
♪ We got the cores ♪

00:09:24.397 --> 00:09:26.299
