00:12:06.158 --> 00:12:08.227
So, unfortunately, no
doggo wars in this episode,

00:12:08.227 --> 00:12:11.130
but here are the pictures
of Paul and Luda.

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:13.933
Here's a picture of ice cream.

00:12:13.933 --> 00:12:15.167
Can someone in graphics make it look

00:12:15.167 --> 00:12:16.736
like they're eating the ice cream?

00:12:19.138 --> 00:12:21.307
Quick clarification before we
start the nutrition section.

00:12:21.307 --> 00:12:22.775
Ice cream is kind of tricky to quantify,

00:12:22.775 --> 00:12:24.443
because sometimes it's
referred to by weight

00:12:24.443 --> 00:12:25.845
and other times by volume.

00:12:25.845 --> 00:12:28.380
It is because the containers
are all the same size, yes,

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:30.449
but the density of ice cream can vary.

00:12:30.449 --> 00:12:33.486
So, overall, seems the fairest
way to measure is by weight.

00:12:33.486 --> 00:12:35.054
In the UK, Ben &amp; Jerry's provides its

00:12:35.054 --> 00:12:37.089
nutritional information per 100 grams,

00:12:37.089 --> 00:12:39.091
whereas in the US they
do it per serving size,

00:12:39.091 --> 00:12:41.861
which is around 141 or 142 grams,

00:12:41.861 --> 00:12:43.929
depending on which type
of ice cream you have.

00:12:43.929 --> 00:12:48.300
So if we divide the US
serving by 1.41 or 1.42,

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:50.436
we should get a roughly
equivalent figure. Got it?

00:12:50.436 --> 00:12:52.171
Let's start with what is officially

00:12:52.171 --> 00:12:55.508
the most popular Ben &amp; Jerry's
flavor in the United States.

00:12:55.508 --> 00:12:57.777
That is this, the Half Baked.

00:12:57.777 --> 00:13:02.381
100 grams of USA's Half
Baked contains 262 calories,

00:13:02.381 --> 00:13:06.619
13.4 grams of fat, 7.8 of
which are saturated fat,

00:13:06.619 --> 00:13:10.756
31.9 grams of carbs, 25.5
grams which are sugar,

00:13:10.756 --> 00:13:13.192
and 90 milligrams of sodium.

00:13:13.192 --> 00:13:16.162
100 grams of UK Half Baked
contains the following:

00:13:16.162 --> 00:13:18.931
264 calories, 13 grams of fat,

00:13:18.931 --> 00:13:21.033
8.1 grams of which is saturated,

00:13:21.033 --> 00:13:22.234
32 grams of carbs,

00:13:22.234 --> 00:13:24.270
of which 27 grams are sugar,

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:25.971
and 84 milligrams of sodium.

00:13:25.971 --> 00:13:27.640
So it looks like the
UK's is actually higher

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:30.676
in saturated fat, carbs,
calories, and sugar,

00:13:30.676 --> 00:13:33.512
although the US edges us
on total fat and sodium.

00:13:33.512 --> 00:13:35.581
What is the most calorific
flavor in the US, you ask?

00:13:35.581 --> 00:13:38.884
Turns out it is the Peanut Butter Cup.

00:13:38.884 --> 00:13:40.786
I couldn't find it.

00:13:40.786 --> 00:13:44.223
This magically delicious
peanut-butter-cup-flavored

00:13:44.223 --> 00:13:47.226
Ben &amp; Jerry's ice cream that
is somewhere in this country,

00:13:47.226 --> 00:13:49.662
100 grams of it contains the following:

00:13:49.662 --> 00:13:50.930
330 calories,

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:52.731
23.3 grams of fat,

00:13:52.731 --> 00:13:54.934
12.6 of those are saturated fat,

00:13:54.934 --> 00:13:56.836
25.3 grams of carbs,

00:13:56.836 --> 00:13:59.104
22.5 grams which are sugar,

00:13:59.104 --> 00:14:02.208
and 126 milligrams of sodium.

00:14:02.208 --> 00:14:04.210
The same ice cream in the UK contains

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:06.512
310 calories, 21 grams of fat,

00:14:06.512 --> 00:14:08.214
of which 12 grams are saturated,

00:14:08.214 --> 00:14:09.381
24 grams of carbs,

00:14:09.381 --> 00:14:11.217
of which 23 grams are sugar,

00:14:11.217 --> 00:14:13.619
and 176 milligrams of sodium.

00:14:13.619 --> 00:14:15.855
This time we edged the
UK on calories, fat,

00:14:15.855 --> 00:14:17.690
saturated fat, and carbs,

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:20.125
while they beat us in sugar and sodium.

00:14:20.125 --> 00:14:22.261
Now, these 100-gram
figures don't seem so bad,

00:14:22.261 --> 00:14:24.630
but bear in mind that they
are for less than one serving.

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.699
Realistically, I'm eating
a whole tub of this

00:14:26.699 --> 00:14:28.033
while cuddled up in my blankets,

00:14:28.033 --> 00:14:29.468
depressed, watching Netflix.

00:14:29.468 --> 00:14:31.036
If you were to eat a whole pint

00:14:31.036 --> 00:14:33.606
of the Peanut Butter Cup ice cream, don't.

00:14:33.606 --> 00:14:35.641
The stats do not look good for you.

00:14:35.641 --> 00:14:37.042
Two figures to watch out for would be

00:14:37.042 --> 00:14:40.246
the 270% of your daily
saturated fat allowance,

00:14:40.246 --> 00:14:43.749
and almost 200% of your daily sugar.

00:14:43.749 --> 00:14:44.817
Blech.

00:14:44.817 --> 00:14:46.085
Here are the numbers for a full tub

00:14:46.085 --> 00:14:47.786
of Peanut Butter Cup in the UK.

00:14:47.786 --> 00:14:48.754
Keep in mind that our tub is

00:14:48.754 --> 00:14:50.990
a tiny bit smaller than
the US one, but overall,

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.192
we are still better off than
them in most of the metrics.

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:55.961
Here is everything that's in a tub

00:14:55.961 --> 00:14:57.162
of Ben &amp; Jerry's Half Baked

00:14:57.162 --> 00:14:58.163
in the UK.
Joe: In the US.

00:14:58.163 --> 00:14:59.365
Harry: Cream, water,
Joe: Cream, liquid sugar,

00:14:59.365 --> 00:15:00.466
Harry: sugar,
Joe: which is sugar and water,

00:15:00.466 --> 00:15:01.433
Harry: condensed skim milk,
Joe: skim milk, water,

00:15:01.433 --> 00:15:02.268
Harry: wheat flour,
Joe: sugar,

00:15:02.268 --> 00:15:03.102
Harry: brown sugar,
Joe: wheat flour,

00:15:03.102 --> 00:15:05.704
[fast-forwarding]

00:15:09.708 --> 00:15:13.345
[fast-forwarding intensifies]

00:15:17.116 --> 00:15:18.284
Seamless.

00:15:18.284 --> 00:15:20.019
These are actually pretty
much identical lists,

00:15:20.019 --> 00:15:21.387
so good job, Ben &amp; Jerry.

00:15:21.387 --> 00:15:22.221
There's also nothing in there

00:15:22.221 --> 00:15:24.089
which you should be
particularly concerned about.

00:15:24.089 --> 00:15:25.524
And this is kind of in
line with Ben &amp; Jerry's

00:15:25.524 --> 00:15:27.593
overall philosophy about
sourcing ingredients.

00:15:27.593 --> 00:15:28.827
According to the Ben &amp; Jerry's website,

00:15:28.827 --> 00:15:31.163
they boast that their
ice cream is non-GMO,

00:15:31.163 --> 00:15:32.998
fair trade, and cage-free.

00:15:32.998 --> 00:15:34.566
And they do seem to live up to that.

00:15:34.566 --> 00:15:37.002
All you "Food Wars" heads
watching this episode

00:15:37.002 --> 00:15:38.737
know that we always have to deal with

00:15:38.737 --> 00:15:40.739
artificial flavors that are OK in the US

00:15:40.739 --> 00:15:42.241
but not allowed in the European Union.

00:15:42.241 --> 00:15:44.276
But the ones that Ben &amp; Jerry use

00:15:44.276 --> 00:15:45.678
are actually made with natural colors,

00:15:45.678 --> 00:15:48.547
like vegetable juice,
spirulina, and turmeric.

00:15:48.547 --> 00:15:49.615
So while what's in the ice cream

00:15:49.615 --> 00:15:50.516
might not be too interesting,

00:15:50.516 --> 00:15:52.484
what's outside it is
actually worth pointing out.

00:15:52.484 --> 00:15:54.320
In the US, the Ben &amp; Jerry pints

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:56.288
do come in a cardboard tub

00:15:56.288 --> 00:15:58.958
that has [polyethylene]
plastic on both sides.

00:15:58.958 --> 00:16:00.826
In the UK, however, they've
actually stopped coating

00:16:00.826 --> 00:16:01.827
the outside of the tubs,

00:16:01.827 --> 00:16:03.595
which makes them more widely recyclable.

00:16:03.595 --> 00:16:05.597
Ben &amp; Jerry's have said
that it is their goal

00:16:05.597 --> 00:16:08.133
to replicate this in the
US at some point this year,

00:16:08.133 --> 00:16:12.071
which would save 79,000
pounds of plastic a year.

00:16:12.071 --> 00:16:12.972
That's it?

00:16:12.972 --> 00:16:14.073
Conner: Got it.
Joe: Got it.

00:16:14.073 --> 00:16:17.876
[laughing] How much chocolate
do I have on my face?

00:16:17.876 --> 00:16:20.646
[Joe singing]

00:16:20.646 --> 00:16:21.480
♪ Ice cream ♪

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:26.018
That looks like my cat after
he's had an upset stomach.

00:16:26.018 --> 00:16:28.354
You know, a little present
he'll leave on the carpet.

